# Nothing here is a requirement source; it keeps local working material and
# anything carrying a credential out of the repository (CLAUDE.md rule 5).

# --- The local toolchain, installed by `just setup` ---
/.venv/

# --- Local scratch: test state roots, volume mounts, and game content ---
# One ignored root, so a local test never has to invent a new ignore rule.
# Game content downloaded outside an image build lives here too: it is
# multi-gigabyte and belongs in a registry, never in git history.
/.local/

# --- Environment files ---
# Runtime configuration and test credentials. Committed examples carry
# obvious placeholders and end in `.example`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Tool caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Implementation-side working material ---
# Reviewer agents write their reports here and assume the directory is
# ignored: an untracked report otherwise fails every clean-tree precondition
# the handover and approval rituals check.
.claude/reviews/
# Agent worktrees are checkouts of this repository inside itself. Tracking
# them would swallow an agent's working copy into an unrelated commit.
.claude/worktrees/
# Operator-local instructions, deliberately not shared.
CLAUDE.local.md
